    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Quiet Ground</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>Everyone is owed a bell. The dead of every people are given a grave and rung for once, friend and foe alike, because the ground keeps what it is given and gives back what it is not. Those who did the killing owe the burying most of all. The bell-keepers keep the rites and listen to the ground, and they are heard before anyone. Ysolde Marr buried the raiders nobody else would and rang her cracked bell over every grave until the fields were quiet, and the Bell has been ringing since.</ideoDescription>
