  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release D"): the bell-keepers' habit is the order's own, an undyed grey
    robe (or with Vanilla Factions Expanded - Medieval 2 a mantle) and a grey veil, worn old or new; its cut and its age
    free. The sextons, who dig, dress plainly and differently around a grey hood: shirts and trousers, packs (Vanilla
    Apparel Expanded - Accessories), caps (Medieval 2); spades (Vanilla Weapons Expanded's shovel), clubs and knives.
    The gravewardens, their guards, share one kit: a helmet and the grey cape over padding (Vanilla Armour Expanded's
    gambesons and quilted vests), with maces, hammers and axes; in the industrial and spacer ages a flamer or a firebomb
    for what will not stay down. A few bell-keepers are A RimWorld of Magic's priests (the first bell most of all), a
    few gravewardens paladins, now and then a sexton a geomancer. They carry linen for shrouds or herbs. Without any mod:
    robes, hoods, capes and helmets, shirts and trousers; clubs, knives, spears and maces.
  -->
